            "content": "<h2>🧺 Care Instructions </h2><p>To ensure the longevity and fit of your apparel, please follow these gentle care steps:</p><ol><li><strong>Wash Cold:</strong> Always turn the garment inside out and wash using a <strong>cold water setting</strong> (gentle cycle) with a mild detergent. This prevents shrinking and preserves color vibrancy.</li><li><strong>Air Dry is Best:</strong> For zero shrinkage, lay flat or hang to air dry. If you must machine dry, use the <strong>lowest heat setting</strong> possible and remove while still slightly damp.</li><li><strong>Avoid High Heat:</strong> High temperatures in washing or drying are the main cause of shrinkage in cotton fibers.</li></ol>"
